{"title":"2025 AIME I Problems/Problem 3","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Video_solution_grogg007\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video solution grogg007</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_1_by_SpreadTheMathLove\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 1 by SpreadTheMathLove</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_-_Using_Combinatorics_to_find_total_assignments_by_HungryCalculator\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution - Using Combinatorics to find total assignments by HungryCalculator</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution(Super_Fun_and_Easy!)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution(Super Fun and Easy!)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Mathletes_Corner\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Mathletes Corner</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_yjtest\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">12</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by yjtest</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-13\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">13</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> members of a baseball team went to an ice-cream parlor after their game. Each player had a single scoop cone of chocolate, vanilla, or strawberry ice cream. At least one player chose each flavor, and the number of players who chose chocolate was greater than the number of players who chose vanilla, which was greater than the number of players who chose strawberry. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> be the number of different assignments of flavors to players that meet these conditions. Find the remainder when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> is divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/4/6b434ebc2071e706df740975a3c90aad3cfa1455.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1000.$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"39\" height=\"13\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_solution_grogg007\">Video solution <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=User:Grogg007\" title=\"User:Grogg007\">grogg007</a></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Video solution grogg007\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/PNBxBvvjbcU?t=231\">https://youtu.be/PNBxBvvjbcU?t=231</a> \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> be the number of players who choose chocolate, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/f/a9f23bf124b6b2b2a993eb313c72e678664ac74a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$v$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> be the number of players who choose vanilla, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> be the number of players who choose strawberry ice cream. We are given three pieces of information <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/4/8a421e87dc0162d79acdd2ef1390a9de1eaf5949.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c,v,s\\ge 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"77\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/6/c36af61d0f98e0de4fde5aba0e4a90a7b345b8fe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c+v+s=9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"105\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/7/ca77b1675becaa1d8cd6814022dc7a7d4d99ebb0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c&gt;v&gt;s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"76\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p>By inspection the only solutions for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/2/852b1e7b7876b6a3d056fb8ae2e30cad07927f8a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(c,v,s)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"58\" height=\"20\" /> are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/7/eb77745fb00b3ca5bd473158f9eaf97c3b87ffd5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(4,3,2),(5,3,1), (6, 2, 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"191\" height=\"20\" /> \n</p><p>Now we must choose which player chooses which flavor. For the general case <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/3/3e351c81f4fb1f0bb45a171a49dc3a5f8892a049.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(c,v,s),$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"63\" height=\"20\" /> we begin by choose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> players who eat chocolate, then we choose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/f/a9f23bf124b6b2b2a993eb313c72e678664ac74a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$v$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/2/6221281e0eab63c05adcaf37a3cb6e01188eb029.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9-c$\" width=\"39\" height=\"12\" /> players who eat vanilla, after this the amount of players who eat strawberry is fixed. Therefore the general formula is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/0/1f0276234c94c045577ccea607b7b541f1eb6504.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\binom{9}{c}\\binom{9-c}{v}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"111\" height=\"55\" />\n</p><p>Therefore our final answer is, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/2/ba26a181c9d099d8f51e9ced413364e722cf889b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\binom{9}{4}\\binom{9-4}{3} + \\binom{9}{5}\\binom{9-5}{3} + \\binom{9}{6}\\binom{9-6}{2} = \\binom{9}{4}\\binom{5}{3} + \\binom{9}{5}\\binom{4}{3} + \\binom{9}{6}\\binom{3}{2} = 2\\boxed{016}\\]\" width=\"689\" height=\"53\" />\n</p><p>Alternatively, this can be written in multinomial coefficients as \n</p>\n<pre><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/a/52a948fc2f8cd6a24cd53db0a58eb2d88415a01f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\binom{9}{4,3,2} + \\binom{9}{5, 3, 1} + \\binom{9}{6, 2, 1}\\]\" width=\"251\" height=\"53\" /> \n</pre>\n<p>which gives the same answer\n</p><p>~ <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=User:Mathkiddus\" title=\"User:Mathkiddus\">mathkiddus</a>\n~ sujoybec51 multiple edits to make more clear\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We apply casework on the scoops the team gets.\n</p><p><u>Case 1:</u> The scoops are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/1/cb1447cd9bfe65e588c9d0e4827c8c7391402587.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6,2,1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"45\" height=\"17\" />. Then we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/f/55f35706e490dbb36b8e9eacafbe57928519774f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\binom{9}{6}\\cdot \\binom{3}{2} = 252$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"141\" height=\"55\" />.\n</p><p><u>Case 2:</u> The scoops are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/f/2cf847d91d41fefc50087f242d39197d2a46af70.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5,3,1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"45\" height=\"17\" />. Then we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/3/e83131196042c82e1a496697bc9e3ca44aceea44.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\binom{9}{5}\\cdot \\binom{4}{3} = 504$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"141\" height=\"55\" />.\n</p><p><u>Case 3:</u> The scoops are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/f/bafd793313a69382f84ce8128f06f1777b00b4fe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4,3,2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"45\" height=\"17\" />. Then we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/f/b4ffd105ad76cd9127acb3b2d2e8641cd1d33ea8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\binom{9}{4}\\cdot \\binom{5}{3} = 1260$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"150\" height=\"55\" />.\n</p><p>Thus the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/a/b4a8993a33557d597ae76c1eaf69c76f67028f3e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$252+504+1260=2\\boxed{016}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"209\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>~ <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=User:Zhenghua\" title=\"User:Zhenghua\">zhenghua</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Denote the number of people who chose strawberry, vanilla, or chocolate as (S, V, C). Then, as S &lt; V &lt; C, we just need to find values of S, V, and C such that S + V + C = 9. Notice S can only be 1 or 2 as S = 3 will result in V + C = 6 and it just won't work for S &lt; V &lt; C. So using these two values, we get that the possible triples of (S, V, C) are: (1, 3, 5), (2, 3, 4) and (1, 2, 6). Now, let's consider (S, V, C) = (1, 3, 5). If we start with the strawberry people, notice there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/7/4475130317aed01a1acdf966cd89d7323c608441.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${9\\choose 1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"39\" height=\"55\" /> possibilities.\nNow, we see there are 8 different people waiting to be assigned to the 3 vanilla people therefore there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/1/b31c1e81941cfae0dadd5ecc65fba793c0ea593a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${8\\choose 3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"39\" height=\"55\" /> ways for this to work. We can now go down the list to get:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/2/f62252af0fbed98ab3a589baa70d60226531c35f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${9\\choose 1}{8\\choose 3}{5\\choose 5} + {9\\choose 2}{7\\choose 3}{4\\choose 4} + {9\\choose 1}{8\\choose 2}{6\\choose 6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"381\" height=\"55\" /> which gives a grand total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/7/4b781fdf1cd172b567be38e2ffa6f20f0b8390c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2016$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"13\" /> possibilities. The remainder when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> is divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/e/6ee927e1332358c96c62c277441c907c4f51057f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/9/8d9da847dc164c20541513495aba09b2d917a666.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{016}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p>~ilikemath247365\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We start by finding the only 3 possible cases, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/9/a19acaf5805e133644c209eaaa26e4c765511154.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C&gt;V&gt;S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"91\" height=\"15\" />. We arrive at\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/6/12644f5792f6e631097f52e78ec00c49f815ee36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(6, 2, 1) = {9 \\choose 6,2,1} = \\frac{9 \\cdot 8 \\cdot 7 \\cdot 6!}{6! \\cdot 2! \\cdot 1!} = 252$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"316\" height=\"55\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/0/2907bf532262a4023341f181da26fba10a837401.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(5, 3, 1) = {9 \\choose 5,3,1} = \\frac{9 \\cdot 8 \\cdot 7 \\cdot 6 \\cdot 5!}{5! \\cdot 3! \\cdot 1!} = 504$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"338\" height=\"55\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/8/b28ad0706c52f54223179b1891b86e4092737b41.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(4, 3, 2) = {9 \\choose 4,3,2} = \\frac{9 \\cdot 8 \\cdot 7 \\cdot 6 \\cdot 5 \\cdot 4!}{4! \\cdot 3! \\cdot 2!} = 1260$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"369\" height=\"55\" />\n</p><p>Summing these up, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/b/07ba8e62aec36970ee6c542b5d093eea938f29be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$252+504+1260= 2\\boxed{016}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"209\" height=\"25\" />\n</p><p>~shreyan.chethan, cleaned up by cweu001 and dareckolo\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5\">Solution 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/0/e20cd0013352e2188ae08a028c8698fef7fbce66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c, v, s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"44\" height=\"13\" /> be chocolate, vanilla, and strawberry respectively. We will also use the notation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/8/04885e691ff18e6c474cbf9f5c9e3ca60c9d8f9b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(s, v, c)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"58\" height=\"20\" /> to denote the number of chocolate, vanilla, and strawberry respectively. We have this condition, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/7/ca77b1675becaa1d8cd6814022dc7a7d4d99ebb0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c&gt;v&gt;s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"76\" height=\"13\" />. Now, we can list out the cases since there wont be a lot. First, we have: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/e/39ed09ec6fcf53b15b31a856f74c07b052392fd6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(1,2,6) \\Longrightarrow \\binom{9}{1} \\cdot \\binom{8}{2} = 252\\]\" width=\"233\" height=\"53\" />. Second, we have: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/c/e3cd357fd1d606032067ea6f92ce895cda81bfc9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(1,3,5) \\Longrightarrow \\binom{9}{1} \\cdot \\binom{8}{3} = 504\\]\" width=\"234\" height=\"53\" />, and last, we have: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/9/1799b8595a8af7987e4db76022327c18cfd381f7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(2,3,4) \\Longrightarrow \\binom{9}{2} \\cdot \\binom{7}{3} = 1260\\]\" width=\"242\" height=\"53\" />. Summing them we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/7/4b781fdf1cd172b567be38e2ffa6f20f0b8390c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2016$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"13\" />, then, we take <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/d/75dc4e3b6f014213e1ebb5ecd2f58ce3ae8b08ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mod 1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"88\" height=\"13\" />, to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/9/8d9da847dc164c20541513495aba09b2d917a666.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{016}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" />\n</p><p>-jb2015007\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_1_by_SpreadTheMathLove\">Video Solution 1 by SpreadTheMathLove</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 1 by SpreadTheMathLove\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=J-0BapU4Yuk\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=J-0BapU4Yuk</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_-_Using_Combinatorics_to_find_total_assignments_by_HungryCalculator\">Video Solution - Using Combinatorics to find total assignments by HungryCalculator</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution - Using Combinatorics to find total assignments by HungryCalculator\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=M0JifQQJtgU\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=M0JifQQJtgU</a>\n</p><p>~HungryCalculator\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution.28Super_Fun_and_Easy.21.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution(Super_Fun_and_Easy!)\">Video Solution(Super Fun and Easy!)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution(Super Fun and Easy!)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/96NUyqcObNo\">https://youtu.be/96NUyqcObNo</a>\n</p><p>~MC\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Mathletes_Corner\">Video Solution by Mathletes Corner</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Mathletes Corner\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Sgeyj5HrnhQ\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Sgeyj5HrnhQ</a>\n</p><p>~GP102\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_yjtest\">Video Solution by yjtest</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by yjtest\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dkG9dN9uuNI\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dkG9dN9uuNI</a>\n</p><p>~yjtest\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=13\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</s